@tempo 98
@swing 0.55
@fx vinyl 0.18
@fx reverb 0.28
@fx lowpass 0.62
@instrument lead pluck
@instrument bass slap
@instrument chord stab

// West African / Afrobeat lofi: C major pentatonic (C D E G A)
// Polyrhythmic groove, call-and-response melody, Andalusian-inspired bass walk

kick:   x x x x . . x . x . . . x . . .
snare:  . . . . x . . . . . x . . . x .
hat:    x . x x x . x . x . x x x . x .
clap:   . . . . x . . x . . . . x . . .
perc:   . x . . . . x . . x . . . . x .

bass:   C2 . E2 . G2 . A2 . G2 . E2 . C2 .
        A1 . C2 . D2 . E2 . G2 . A2 . G2 .
        C2 . D2 . E2 . G2 . A2 . G2 . E2 .
        G2 . A2 . G2 . E2 . D2 . C2 . . .

lead:   C4 D4 E4 G4 A4 G4 E4 D4
        C4 . G3 . A3 C4 D4 E4
        G4 A4 G4 E4 D4 E4 D4 C4
        D4 E4 G4 . A4 G4 E4 .

        G4 A4 C5 A4 G4 E4 D4 C4
        E4 D4 C4 D4 E4 G4 A4 G4
        E4 D4 E4 G4 A4 G4 E4 D4
        C4 . D4 E4 G4 E4 C4 .

chords: C Am F G
        C Am F G

// Kick: syncopated Afrobeat clave feel (3+3+2)
// Hat: 16th-note throws on beats 2 and 3 give the Afropop bounce
// Bass: pentatonic walk, always returns to C root
// Lead: call (ascend C→A) and response (descend A→C), classic West African phrasing
